From 79a0a6aa5ab8ccda09d05d026ff29145a25f15da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonardo Tada Antunes <leonardotada@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:01:01 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] Sweep one block at a time

The sweep used to hold the page filler mutex for the whole heap. It now visits
one block per lock acquisition (scan, free dead extents, then a separate
minimize pass), inserts the swept slabs into the bins as it goes, and keeps a
cursor over the ring of blocks that is fixed up when a block leaves it. The
world is still stopped by probation, so behaviour is unchanged: unit tests,
the Phobos stress and the benchmark gate pass, also with the verifier.
